s contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 109 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.828 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a mercados estables o necesidades específicas. No refleja actos ilícitos ni errores.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] abordan necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en años distintos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen por sectores o servicios específicos.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 125 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 19.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.8 to 8.3. Contract [1], for 14,828 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["u0GWN3ThEKg%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D","IgK7rCDutyOLAncw3qdZkA%3D%3D","oKIXAnVq440wYTJJ03sHog%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}